1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,569
Good morning, Synmouth Museum.

2
00:00:02,569 --> 00:00:03,600
Can I help you?

3
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:04,437
Oh yes.

4
00:00:04,437 --> 00:00:05,273
Good morning.

5
00:00:05,273 --> 00:00:11,130
I'm interested in the children's workshops and I'd like a little more information, please.

6
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:13,740
Do you mean the Art and Craft workshops?

7
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:14,079
Yes.

8
00:00:14,079 --> 00:00:18,831
A friend of a friend mentioned them-the children do painting and make models and

9
00:00:18,831 --> 00:00:19,510
so forth.

10
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:21,032
Yes, of course.

11
00:00:21,032 --> 00:00:23,061
Um, where to begin?

12
00:00:23,061 --> 00:00:28,640
First of all, as you probably know, they run every Saturday.

13
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:29,246
Fine.

14
00:00:29,246 --> 00:00:31,670
And what about ages?

15
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:36,716
Well, all ages from five upwards are welcome, though we do ask that children

16
00:00:36,716 --> 00:00:40,320
below eight years of age are accompanied by an adult.

17
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:40,777
Fine.

18
00:00:40,777 --> 00:00:43,060
That wouldn't be a problem.

19
00:00:43,060 --> 00:00:44,430
What about cost?

20
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:47,559
Well, I think you'll find them very reasonable.

21
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:51,862
It's ￡2.50 a child, with 80 pence off for two

22
00:00:51,862 --> 00:00:54,600
or more children from the same family.

23
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:56,260
Oh yes, very reasonable.

24
00:00:56,260 --> 00:00:59,580
And are they held in the main museum?

25
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:01,020
Not exactly.

26
00:01:01,020 --> 00:01:02,460
They're nearby.

27
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:04,800
Could you give me the full address?

28
00:01:04,800 --> 00:01:07,140
I don't know the area very well.

29
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:10,540
Yes, it's Winter House.

30
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:11,790
Right.

31
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:15,360
And that's in Tamer Street.

32
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,530
Could you spell that please?

33
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:23,620
Yes, T-A-M-E-R Street.

34
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:24,960
Lovely.

35
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:29,126
And I do need to tell you that there's a security entrance,

36
00:01:29,126 --> 00:01:33,987
so you need to press the green button for someone to let you in.

37
00:01:33,987 --> 00:01:36,070
Don't press the red button please,

38
00:01:36,070 --> 00:01:38,500
but don't worry, it's all clearly labelled.

39
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:38,986
OK.

40
00:01:38,986 --> 00:01:42,388
And one more question-is parking available nearby?

41
00:01:42,388 --> 00:01:45,790
We're driving in from out of town.

42
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:50,597
Your best bet is to leave your car at the back of the library-on

43
00:01:50,597 --> 00:01:53,687
a Saturday morning there are plenty of spaces there.

44
00:01:53,687 --> 00:01:56,090
It's right next door to the museum.

45
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:59,650
And can I ask about booking places?

46
00:01:59,650 --> 00:02:00,070
Yes,

47
00:02:00,070 --> 00:02:05,950
and I must tell you, you really should book by calling the education department

48
00:02:05,950 --> 00:02:06,370
here.

49
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:11,900
Oh, I'm sorry, should I have rung them instead of the main museum number?

50
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:12,392
No,

51
00:02:12,392 --> 00:02:15,835
that's fine this time, please don't worry.

52
00:02:15,835 --> 00:02:20,754
But for future reference, I'll give you the direct number.

53
00:02:20,754 --> 00:02:22,230
It's two hundred-seven-six-five.

54
00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:24,420
Great, I've got that.

55
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:31,590
But I'm very happy to give you information about the next two workshops.

56
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:35,450
On Saturday the 16th there's Building Castles.

57
00:02:35,450 --> 00:02:37,330
Oh, sounds great!

58
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:39,665
This involves quite a bit of glue,

59
00:02:39,665 --> 00:02:43,000
so just make sure the kids are in old clothes.

60
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,940
I know, ones I don't mind getting mucky.

61
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:46,308
Exactly.

62
00:02:46,308 --> 00:02:51,460
And if possible, could you bring along bottle tops which the children might be

63
00:02:51,460 --> 00:02:55,140
able to use in the models, you know, as decoration?

64
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:57,730
We'll certainly try to find some for you.

65
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:00,110
Then the following week...

66
00:03:00,110 --> 00:03:02,740
That'll be the 23rd, won't it?

67
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:03,166
Yes,

68
00:03:03,166 --> 00:03:04,018
that's right.

69
00:03:04,018 --> 00:03:07,852
On that day, it's what we call Undersea Worlds.

70
00:03:07,852 --> 00:03:13,390
This is where they make scenes with fishes, underground caverns and so on.

71
00:03:13,390 --> 00:03:16,215
IS that likely to get very dirty?

72
00:03:16,215 --> 00:03:17,830
Lots of paint splashes?

73
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:18,500
Not really,

74
00:03:18,500 --> 00:03:21,852
so we don't recommend any special clothes for that one.

75
00:03:21,852 --> 00:03:26,543
But if you could search out some silver paper to bring along to use

76
00:03:26,543 --> 00:03:29,895
in the sessions, you know, it's shiny-it looks like water,

77
00:03:29,895 --> 00:03:30,900
that'd be great.

78
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:31,877
Yes, of course.

79
00:03:31,877 --> 00:03:34,483
We'll see what we can come up with.

80
00:03:34,483 --> 00:03:37,740
Well, thank you ever so much for all your help.

81
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:42,300
The sessions sound really good and I'll certainly book up for the next two.

82
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:42,823
Lovely.

83
00:03:42,823 --> 00:03:45,440
Thanks very much for ringing.

84
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,410
Bye.

85
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:47,560
Bye-bye.
